1
00:00:02,198 --> 00:00:04,349
Now that's it for this module. We

2
00:00:04,365 --> 00:00:05,280
implemented the

3
00:00:06,355 --> 00:00:09,132
MVC pattern

4
00:00:09,887 --> 00:00:11,411
and we also had a look at CRUD.

5
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:14,766
CRUD were these 4 operations: creating,

6
00:00:14,878 --> 00:00:16,788
reading, updating, and deleting, which you

7
00:00:16,788 --> 00:00:19,517
need in almost all applications you're going

8
00:00:19,597 --> 00:00:19,982
to build.

9
00:00:20,576 --> 00:00:22,903
And you also saw how CRUD and MVC work

10
00:00:22,903 --> 00:00:25,600
together by passing data around and by using

11
00:00:25,632 --> 00:00:27,783
a model for storing and fetching and

12
00:00:27,863 --> 00:00:29,387
updating your data.

13
00:00:30,028 --> 00:00:32,498
We're still only storing data in a dummy

14
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:35,255
variable which is lost as soon as the app

15
00:00:35,319 --> 00:00:38,173
reloads, but we'll fix and improve that in

16
00:00:38,206 --> 00:00:39,424
the database module.

17
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:42,278
One other important thing which we saw in

18
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:43,384
this module here

19
00:00:43,978 --> 00:00:47,088
is the use of dynamic route segments, as

20
00:00:47,265 --> 00:00:49,445
here for getting a single element or for

21
00:00:49,445 --> 00:00:50,712
deleting an element.

22
00:00:51,449 --> 00:00:54,880
Such dynamic segments enable you to set up

23
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:58,680
routes that work with any kind of data, for

24
00:00:58,728 --> 00:01:01,676
example, with any kind of goal ID to then

25
00:01:01,772 --> 00:01:04,464
return that ID, delete that ID, or whatever

26
00:01:04,496 --> 00:01:06,307
your application might need to do.

27
00:01:06,916 --> 00:01:09,447
And with that, we got all the core knowledge

28
00:01:09,479 --> 00:01:12,203
and all the core features of Deno and Oak

29
00:01:12,348 --> 00:01:15,777
covered that enable us to build more amazing

30
00:01:15,889 --> 00:01:16,578
applications.

31
00:01:17,315 --> 00:01:20,712
So as a next step, I would suggest that we

32
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:23,628
also see how we can use a real database.
